  "name": "Kalobos",
  "type": "deity",
  "effects": [],
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\">Category: Seen Gods</em></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><em>Espirian Domains: The Hells (Arcanum)</em></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Kalobos is the ruler of the Forest of Burning Brambles, where devils reign and punish those who have disobeyed the laws of the wood. Amongst many of Kalobos’ edicts is to turn the nature of mankind’s laws into a chafing, thorny rose that bleeds all who follow it. His realm is the perversion of the concept of Order itself. In that way, many devils follow him and seek to torment and twist just societies, offering to aid lawmakers and even druids who respect and value pacts by writing their contracts and terms. The cost, which is often the souls of those who seek their services, also comes to chafe and enchain all those who fall under those laws.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Title </strong>Deer of Cosmic Order</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\">Edicts</strong> Adhere the laws of nature and subject lands to law, punish its violators</span><span style=\"mso-tab-count:1\">      </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\">Anathema </strong>renege and give mercy outside the statement of the law, change the terms of contracts and laws</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Areas of Concern</strong> Law, Nature, Order</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Religious Symbol</strong> A bleeding heart chafed by thorny vines</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Sacred Animal</strong> Deer</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Sacred Colors</strong> green and red</span></p>"
